Compare a temperature below the limit:
```javascript
const temperature = 17;
const limit = 19;
const below = temperature < limit;
const atLimit = temperature === limit;
const above = temperature > limit;
console.log(below, atLimit, above);
```
Output:
```text
true false false
```
17 is below 19, not equal to it, and not above it. Commas let `console.log` show all three answers.

A boundary is the exact point where an answer changes. Try the temperature exactly at the limit:
```javascript
const temperature = 19;
const limit = 19;
console.log(temperature < limit);
console.log(temperature === limit);
console.log(temperature > limit);
console.log(temperature >= limit);
```
Output:
```text
false
true
false
true
```
19 is not greater than 19, but it is greater than or equal to 19.
